{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.PairEnergyRewardsShort","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.PairEnergyRewardsShort","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PairEnergyRewardsShort.neg_kernel_of_nonsingleton_minimiser","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PairEnergyRewardsShort.neg_kernel_of_nonsingleton_minimiser","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PairEnergyRewardsShort.lean#L122-L129","doc":"Contrapositive, and the useful one for design: if a pair energy is to\nselect something LONGER than one letter, the kernel must take a negative value\nsomewhere. Stated as the exact obstruction rather than as advice. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PairEnergyRewardsShort.exists_singleton_minimiser","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PairEnergyRewardsShort.exists_singleton_minimiser","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PairEnergyRewardsShort.lean#L109-L120","doc":"The form that bites on a selection program: if the catalogue contains ANY\none-letter word, the program's optimum is `0` and is attained there, whatever\nelse the catalogue holds.\n\nThis is why the measured degeneracy is structural. It is also exactly why the\nhonest comparison is at FIXED length, where every candidate has the same number\nof pairs and the kernel's separation-dependence is what decides. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PairEnergyRewardsShort.pairEnergy_singleton_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PairEnergyRewardsShort.pairEnergy_singleton_le","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PairEnergyRewardsShort.lean#L98-L107","doc":"**\"Rewards short operators\", proved.**\n\nUnder a non-negative kernel, a one-letter word is a GLOBAL minimiser of the\npair energy — it attains `0` and nothing can go below `0`. So minimising a pair\nenergy over a catalogue of mixed lengths selects a shortest operator for a\nreason that has nothing to do with the operator: the sum is empty. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PairEnergyRewardsShort.pairEnergy_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PairEnergyRewardsShort.pairEnergy_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PairEnergyRewardsShort.lean#L88-L96","doc":"A pair energy built from a non-negative kernel is non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PairEnergyRewardsShort.headPairs_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PairEnergyRewardsShort.headPairs_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PairEnergyRewardsShort.lean#L79-L86","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PairEnergyRewardsShort.pairEnergy_singleton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PairEnergyRewardsShort.pairEnergy_singleton","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PairEnergyRewardsShort.lean#L73-L77","doc":"**A one-letter word has no pairs, so its pair energy is exactly `0`** — for\nevery kernel, definitionally. This is the fact the probe observed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PairEnergyRewardsShort.pairEnergy_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PairEnergyRewardsShort.pairEnergy_nil","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PairEnergyRewardsShort.lean#L71-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PairEnergyRewardsShort.pairEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PairEnergyRewardsShort.pairEnergy","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PairEnergyRewardsShort.lean#L66-L69","doc":"The discretised pair energy: a sum over ordered pairs of the word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PairEnergyRewardsShort.headPairs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PairEnergyRewardsShort.headPairs","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PairEnergyRewardsShort.lean#L59-L64","doc":"Pairs of a head letter with each later letter, carrying the separation.\nMirrors the probe's `E_pair` inner loop and\n`QBeta.ECatProbeAssertions.headPairs`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}